From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charlie <5764343+charlielye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:09:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(txe): run the world state and the AVM in memory, on
 wsdb-ref and bb-avm-sim's wasm module

Each session runs wsdb-ref and the AVM's wasm module on one worker: the AVM
reaches the world state there as a synchronous call, and the session's contract
DB through the AVM pool's CDB dispatch, answered on the session's thread. No
aztec-wsdb or bb-avm-sim process and no world state on disk.
TXE_WORLD_STATE=native runs the processes as before.

- world-state: IpcWorldState takes any service over the wsdb API, and
  NativeWorldStateService.fromService starts one at a genesis sent over
  InitGenesis.
- simulator: the CDB server opens its socket only when a process asks for its
  path, and spawners also get its dispatch for an AVM in this process.
- txe: depends on wsdb-ref, bb-avm-sim and ipc-runtime, kept out of the bundle
  since they load wasm and worker scripts beside their own modules.
- wsdb-ref is portalled by use-local and pinned like bb-avm-sim.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G5s7nEWrYapDK2CWpEzcAf

